# ============================================================================
# SMARTHUB CONNECT — ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (for local dev) or set these in the Vercel
# dashboard (for production). NEVER commit your real .env.local to GitHub.
#
# How to use on Vercel:
#   1. Go to your project → Settings → Environment Variables
#   2. Add each variable below with its real value
#   3. Redeploy
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE (Prisma)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite file path for local dev. On Vercel, use a real database like Postgres
# (Vercel Postgres, Supabase, Neon, etc.) and update prisma/schema.prisma
# to change the datasource provider from "sqlite" to "postgresql".
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTACT FORM (Formspree)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign up at https://formspree.io and create a new form.
# They'll give you an endpoint like https://formspree.io/f/abcd1234
# Put that here. Without this, the contact form will show an error message.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT="https://formspree.io/f/your-form-id"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROOM BOOKING DATABASE (Supabase)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run supabase/schema.sql in the Supabase SQL editor first, then copy these
# two values from Project Settings -> API.
#
# Unlike the Google Form, the database can refuse a double booking: two people
# cannot hold the same room at the same time, whatever the browser sends.
#
# This key is MEANT to be public - it ships in the JavaScript bundle. Row
# level security (supabase/schema.sql section 8) is what protects the data:
# with this key you may create a pending booking and read the room list, and
# nothing else. See docs/supabase-keys.md for where to find these.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project-ref.supabase.co"

# SET ONE OF THESE TWO - whichever your project has. They do the same job.
#
#   Newer projects (created from Nov 2025) have a PUBLISHABLE key that looks
#   like sb_publishable_xxxxx. Use this one:
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_your-key-here"
#
#   Older projects have an ANON key instead: a long JWT starting with eyJ...
#   Still works, but Supabase is removing it at the end of 2026.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-anon-public-key"

# The secret / service_role key bypasses ALL security - it ignores every row
# level security rule and can read every customer's details. Only ever use it
# in server-side code, and NEVER prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ (that would ship
# it to the browser). This site does not need it; leave it unset.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY="sb_secret_your-key-here"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROOM BOOKING (Google Form)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The booking page (#/book) submits straight into the team's existing Google
# Form "Application for SmartHub Room Booking", so every request still lands
# in the same response sheet.
#
# You only need this variable if the form is ever RECREATED (a new form gets
# a new id). Leave it unset to use the id baked into src/lib/booking-data.ts.
#
# Where to find the id: open the live form and copy the long "1FAIpQLS..."
# segment out of the URL:
#   https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/<THIS_PART>/viewform
#
# IMPORTANT: if you recreate the form you must ALSO update the `entry.<id>`
# numbers in src/lib/booking-data.ts (GOOGLE_FORM.entry). Get them from the
# form's "Get pre-filled link" option.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_FORM_ID="1FAIpQLSf--kAyGYvX2S7mtPz4pIbam2SaLat7fPLEHpR5bcgcqw1aQg"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANALYTICS (optional — Plausible)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sign up at https://plausible.io, add your site, and put the domain here.
# Then uncomment the Plausible script in src/app/layout.tsx
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN="smarthubc.com"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEWSLETTER (optional — Mailchimp / ConvertKit / Loops)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When you wire up the newsletter form in src/components/pages/insights.tsx
# to a real provider, put the API endpoint here.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NEWSLETTER_ENDPOINT="https://manage.kmail-lists.com/..."